{"id":"topaz","name":"Topaz","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:topaz"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Topaz","text":"Heb. pitdah (Ezek. 28:13; Rev. 21:20), a golden yellow or “green” stone brought from Cush or Ethiopia (Job 28:19). It was the second stone in the first row in the breastplate of the high priest, and had the name of Simeon inscribed on it (Ex. 28:17). It is probably the chrysolite of the moderns."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H6357","lemma":"פִּטְדָה","xlit":"piṭdâh","gloss":"a gem, probably the topaz","kjv":"topaz","count":4,"share":0.8},{"strong":"H124","lemma":"אֹדֶם","xlit":"ʼôdem","gloss":"redness","kjv":"sardius","count":3,"share":0.6},{"strong":"H1304","lemma":"בָּרֶקֶת","xlit":"bâreqeth","gloss":"a gem , perhaps the emerald","kjv":"carbuncle","count":3,"share":0.6},{"strong":"H68","lemma":"אֶבֶן","xlit":"ʼeben","gloss":"a stone","kjv":"carbuncle, mason, plummet, stone","count":3,"share":0.6},{"strong":"H2905","lemma":"טוּר","xlit":"ṭûwr","gloss":"a row","kjv":"row","count":2,"share":0.4},{"strong":"H4390","lemma":"מָלֵא","xlit":"mâlêʼ","gloss":"to fill or be full of, in a wide application","kjv":"accomplish, confirm, consecrate, be at an end","count":2,"share":0.4}],"verses":["Exod.28.17","Exod.39.10","Job.28.19","Ezek.28.13","Rev.21.20"],"related":[{"id":"sardius","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.667,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"carbuncle","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.5,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"precious-stones","type":"cooccur","shared":5,"jaccard":0.078,"why":"5 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"stones","type":"cooccur","shared":4,"jaccard":0.028,"why":"4 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"carbuncle","type":"lexical","strong":"H124","why":"both lead with אֹדֶם (H124)"},{"id":"sardius","type":"lexical","strong":"H124","why":"both lead with אֹדֶם (H124)"}],"works":[{"work":"anf02","title":"Ante-Nicene Fathers, Volume 2: Fathers of the Secon